# Getting started with {{ project_name }}

This guide sets up everything you need to author and verify contract-driven
agents: the Python environment (via **uv**) and the **FizzBee** model checker
(the `fizz` command).

## 1. Prerequisites

| Tool | Why | Install |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Python {{ python_version }}+** | runs the agent and the tooling | [python.org](https://www.python.org/) or `uv python install {{ python_version }}` |
| **uv** | environment + dependency manager | `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh \| sh` (see [docs](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)) |
| **fizz** (FizzBee) | model-checks the contracts | see step 3 |
| **Homebrew** *(macOS/Linux)* | easiest way to install `fizz` | [brew.sh](https://brew.sh/) |

## 2. Python environment

```bash
uv sync
```

`uv sync` reads `pyproject.toml`, creates a `.venv`, and installs both runtime
and dev dependencies (including `pytest` and `lxml`). Run project commands with
`uv run …` so they use that environment — e.g. `uv run pytest -q`.

## 3. Install the FizzBee model checker

The `fizz` binary exhaustively checks that no contract can reach a state that
violates its invariants.

**Homebrew (recommended):**

```bash
brew tap fizzbee-io/fizzbee
brew install fizzbee
fizz --help          # confirm it's on your PATH
```

**Prebuilt binary (alternative):** download a release for your OS from
<https://github.com/fizzbee-io/fizzbee/releases>, extract it, and put the `fizz`
binary on your `PATH`.

> Tip: `fizz install-skills` drops FizzBee's own reference skills into
> `~/.claude/skills/`, which help when writing FizzBee in an agentic editor.

If `fizz` is not installed, `pytest` will *skip* the model-check test with a
clear message, but `make fizz-check` (and therefore `make gate`) will **fail** —
model checking is not optional for a real contract.

## 4. Run the gate

```bash
make gate
```

This runs, in order:

1. `uv run pytest -q` — schema validation + model-check test.
2. `uv run python scripts/verify_fizzbee_contracts.py` — model-checks every `agent_*.xml`.
3. `uv run python scripts/verify_promise_graph.py` — verifies the promise graph.

On a freshly generated project this is **green out of the box** against the toy
`barista` agent — proof that your toolchain is set up correctly before you write
a line of your own.

## 5. Next steps

- Read the two toy contracts in `agent_contracts/` — `agent_barista.xml` (an LLM
  agent, with a FizzBee `<verifiable-behavior>` section) and `manifest_machine.xml` (a non-LLM
  service agent, promise manifest only).
- Follow **"Writing your own agent"** in [README.md](README.md).
- Keep every FizzBee invariant paired with real enforcement code and a test:
  the model check proves the *specification*, never the LLM's *behavior*.
